:\\\"subset of ℝ\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"[0,1].\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"geometry-product-dimension\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is nonempty.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is compact.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"Hausdorff dimension threshold: if d<dim_H(A), then H^d(A)=∞.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"dim_H\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"Hausdorff dimension threshold: if d<dim_H(A), then H^d(A)=∞.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"A is a subset of a Borel extended metric space; d is a nonnegative real.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M001-0001/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"1e2974873151488a644ca1f93451e98bf2f2e911dba567adf7983fa7abfccdb1\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH : ↑d < dimH s → μH[d] s = ∞\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"Lipschitz maps do not increase Hausdorff dimension of images.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"dim_H\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"Lipschitz maps do not increase Hausdorff dimension of images.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"f is Lipschitz between extended metric spaces; s is a subset of the domain.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M002-0002/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"24901487517562f47ec0d40b0915c250514f02599c40979d318f9d92bc9b804e\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le : LipschitzWith K f → dimH (f '' s) ≤ dimH s\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M003\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"A subset of finite-dimensional real normed space with nonempty interior has Hausdorff dimension equal to the finrank.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"dim_H\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"A subset of finite-dimensional real normed space with nonempty interior has Hausdorff dimension equal to the finrank.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"V is a finite-dimensional real normed space and interior(s) is nonempty.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M003-0003/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"c783a006ff20bfe97d7c98bfd5f18d8784ed298de1696686684d298de169668\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Real.dimH_of_nonempty_interior\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"Real.dimH_of_nonempty_interior : Nonempty (interior s) → dimH s = finrank ℝ V\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M004\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"The integral of a countable sum of nonnegative measurable functions equals the sum of their integrals.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"The integral of a countable sum of nonnegative measurable functions equals the sum of their integrals.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"The summands are AEMeasurable ENNReal functions on a measure space and the index type is countable.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M004-0005/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"b0fd457ea61a6a025c9884af4cc4afcff3a4bb6a1649fcb7276fb23108a3a8ff\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Lebesgue.Add\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"14da3dd3c269221e9ec43e91c6b22bb02d5db7f00e03c789661c72dffecf7b4a\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum : (∀i,AEMeasurable (f i) μ) → ∫⁻a, ∑'i,f i a ∂μ = ∑'i,∫⁻a,f i a ∂μ\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"dim_H\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\",\\\"M003\\\",\\\"M004\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"case_elimination\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let D=dim_H(E) and F=E×I. Compactness makes E bounded; ordinary Euclidean cube covers of a bounded box show dim_H(E)≤n, hence D<∞. For q>D, the Hausdorff threshold gives H^q(E)=0. At scale δ≤1 cover E by sets of positive diameters r_j≤δ with arbitrarily small sum of q-powers, replacing singleton members by small positive-diameter balls at arbitrarily small total q-cost. Cover I over each member by at most 1/r_j+1 intervals of length ≤r_j. The products cover F; each diameter is ≤√2r_j and total (q+1)-cost ≤2(√2)^(q+1)Σr_j^q. Costs tend to zero as δ→0, so H^(q+1)(F)=0 and dim_H(F)≤D+1.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H002\\\",\\\"M001\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"n\\\",\\\"q\\\",\\\"δ\\\",\\\"r_j\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"For D>0 fix 0<s<D. The dimension threshold gives H^s(E)=∞, hence scale contents c_s(E,δ) tend to infinity as δ↓0. For any countable cover V_i of F with ρ_i=diam(V_i)≤δ≤1, let A_i,B_i be projections; diameters are ≤ρ_i. Enclose each B_i in an open interval J_i of length ≤ρ_i+η_i with η_i>0 and Ση_iρ_i^s<ε. For each t∈I, the A_i with t∈J_i cover E, since every (x,t) belongs to some V_i and B_i⊆J_i. Thus c_s(E,δ)≤Σ_i 1_{J_i}(t)ρ_i^s pointwise. The interval indicators are measurable, and M004 permits integration of their nonnegative series; integrating over I gives c_s(E,δ)≤Σ_i(ρ_i+η_i)ρ_i^s≤Σ_iρ_i^(s+1)+ε. Zero-diameter terms vanish because s>0. Let ε→0 and infimize over product covers: c_s(E,δ)≤c_(s+1)(F,δ). Therefore H^(s+1)(F)=∞ and dim_H(F)≥s+1. Taking 0<s<D gives dim_H(F)≥D+1.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"s\\\",\\\"δ\\\",\\\"V_i\\\",\\\"ρ_i\\\",\\\"A_i\\\",\\\"B_i\\\",\\\"J_i\\\",\\\"η_i\\\",\\\"ε\\\",\\\"c_s\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"If D=0, choose x₀∈E by H001. The coordinate projection π:F→I is 1-Lipschitz for the concatenated Euclidean distance and is onto because (x₀,t)∈F for each t. M003 gives dim_H(I)=1 because I has nonempty interior in ℝ. M002 gives dim_H(I)≤dim_H(F), so dim_H(F)≥1=D+1. This applies also for n=0. Combining with the upper bound proves the equality.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"M002\\\",\\\"M003\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"x₀\\\",\\\"π\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"n\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Apply in Euclidean Borel space to E with q>D.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Apply in Euclidean Borel space to E with 0<s<D.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"π is 1-Lipschitz in the concatenated metric.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M003\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"I has nonempty interior and finrank ℝ ℝ=1.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M004\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"The summands are ρ_i^s times indicators of open intervals, and are measurable nonnegative functions.\\\"]}]}]}}\"}","status":"completed"}}

